Subject: A command buffer finds a program's state among 256 slots, not 64

The slots are direct-mapped by the program's uid. A frame of the phone's own stages draws with some 45 programs,
and two that share a slot found each other's state gone at every draw: the queue asked again under its lock, the
state's reference copied and pushed onto the buffer's list (StateCache::find and malloc in the profile of scene T).


---
diff --git a/hakios-metal/src/render.cpp b/hakios-metal/src/render.cpp
index 1b9ae44..3e5b3b7 100644
--- a/hakios-metal/src/render.cpp
+++ b/hakios-metal/src/render.cpp
@@ -3228,8 +3228,10 @@ struct DrawCache {
         uint32_t keyId = StateCache::kNoKey;
         const ProgramState* state = nullptr;
     };
-    static constexpr uint32_t kSlots = 64;
-    Slot slots[kSlots];
+    // (as many as a frame has programs several times over: two programs in one slot find each other's state gone at
+    // every draw, and ask the queue again under its lock)
+    static constexpr uint32_t kSlotBits = 8;
+    Slot slots[1u << kSlotBits];
     std::vector<std::shared_ptr<const ProgramState>> kept;   // ...alive until the buffer is done
     // a Program made by hand, as it was when its state was made: a draw with the Program at that address is the same
     // draw only while every byte of it, its immediates and its two addresses in this buffer are the same
@@ -3912,7 +3914,7 @@ bool CommandBuffer::draw(const Program& program, const RenderPass& pass, const D
